  "correction_rules": [
    "Reduce forecast overshoots following strong upward sentiment spikes (e.g., sentiment > 0.20) by 10-15% to avoid overreaction.",
    "Adjust downward forecasts when sentiment is negative (e.g., sentiment < -0.20) by adding a 5-10% buffer to avoid underestimating downside risk.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias correction: if forecast deviates > 10% from recent 5-day average, adjust toward historical mean.",
    "For long-term (30-day) forecasts, reduce volatility in the tail (last 3-5 days) if sentiment is neutral or negative to prevent over-optimism.",
    "When sentiment is positive but recent prices are trending down, slightly dampen forecast growth to avoid lagging the market’s correction.",
    "If forecast consistently overestimates true outcome in early days of a new trend (e.g., first 5 days), apply a 5-10% downward correction to align with sentiment-driven momentum decay."
  ]
}
